9. MITRE ATT&CK Mapping
T1003.001 – OS Credential Dumping: LSASS Memory

The creation of an LSASS memory dump is consistent with OS Credential Dumping: LSASS Memory, where an attacker accesses LSASS memory to obtain credential material.

T1003 – OS Credential Dumping

The observed behavior falls under the broader OS Credential Dumping technique.

10. Overall Findings

The investigation established the following sequence of activity:

Outflank-Dumpert.exe

↓

Attempted LSASS handle duplication

↓

Target object: lsass.exe

↓

Created dumpert.dmp

↓

Additional registry activity

↓

W32Time\SecureTimeLimits

The correlation of these events provides evidence of an LSASS memory-dumping operation.

11. Conclusion

The investigation identified suspicious access to the lsass.exe process by Outflank-Dumpert.exe, followed by creation of the dumpert.dmp memory-dump file.

The combination of LSASS handle duplication and subsequent dump creation is consistent with credential-access activity through LSASS memory dumping.

Additional registry activity involving W32Time\SecureTimeLimits was also observed and attributed to the same executable. This activity has been included in the incident timeline for further investigation and correlation with other available endpoint and security telemetry.

